{
  "rationale": "The plant automata model the robot's perception and motion primitives, with all sensor outcomes as uncontrollable and all motion commands as controllable. The specification automata encode the safe exploration policy: maximize forward/random_walk coverage in clear states, react to obstacles with minimal, directed recovery, and return to exploration as soon as the path is clear. Recovery states are one-shot and deterministic, and full_rotate is reserved for repeated or deadlocked obstacle conditions. Oscillation is avoided by assigning only one rotation direction per obstacle side.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception (sensors) and motion (actuators)",
    "Specification automata bind each perception outcome to a unique, safe, and coverage-oriented motion command, with conservative recovery and rapid return to exploration"
